      en: "Bebris Tsikhe (meaning 'Old Fortress') is a historic fortress near the city of Mtskheta in central Georgia. It sits on a hill overlooking the Mtkvari and Aragvi rivers. The fortress was built in the 9th century and served as a defense for the ancient capital Mtskheta. It consists of a rectangular tower and a surrounding wall. In the 12th century, it was reinforced by King David the Builder. Bebris Tsikhe played a role in the battles against the Mongols in the 13th century. Today, the fortress is partially restored and a popular viewpoint. From here, there is an excellent view of Jvari Monastery and Mtskheta.",
